1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,550
On Mars there's no GPS,
and help can be 22 minutes away.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,300
MarsNav keeps a way home on every step.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,000
It plans each walk on NASA's HiRISE terrain,
safety first.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,600
It scores landing sites
with data from seven NASA missions.

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,750
If a suit leaks,
every display turns the crew home.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,900
Perseverance took 85 sols for this trip.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,700
MarsNav plans it as an 84-minute walk.

8
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,400
Forty simulated walks:
no crew touched their reserve.

9
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,400
MarsNav. Every step, a way home.

